      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case is described where severe hypophosphataemia was induced by a widely used protocol for glucose-insulin-potassium (GIK) infusion. Hypophosphataemia was found to be a universal sequel to the use of this infusion. A new regimen for administering this agent was designed, and shown to lack the potentially serious side effect of phosphate depletion."},
